### Ready-to-run requests (Visual Studio "HTTP file" or the VS Code REST Client extension).
### Change the port to the one your app prints on startup (use the http:// URL to avoid certificate prompts).
@host = http://localhost:5000
@junction = A

### 1. List junctions (with live status)
GET {{host}}/api/junctions

### 2. Junction detail (config + status)
GET {{host}}/api/junctions/{{junction}}

### 3. Create a new junction (same engine, default two-phase plan)
POST {{host}}/api/junctions
Content-Type: application/json

{ "junction_id": "B", "name": "Loading dock junction" }

### 4. Status: desired vs actual signals, queues, mode, alerts, pending command
GET {{host}}/api/junctions/{{junction}}/status

### 5. Vehicle arrival (truck, north)
POST {{host}}/api/sensor-events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "event_id": "evt-10001",
  "junction_id": "A",
  "direction": "NORTH",
  "event_type": "VEHICLE_ARRIVED",
  "vehicle_id": "VH-501",
  "vehicle_type": "TRUCK",
  "sequence_no": 1501,
  "timestamp": "2026-10-08T10:15:20Z"
}

### 6. SAME event again -> 200 DUPLICATE, queue unchanged
### (edit the timestamp of request 5 to "now" if you get 422 "older than 10 min")
POST {{host}}/api/sensor-events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "event_id": "evt-10001",
  "junction_id": "A",
  "direction": "NORTH",
  "event_type": "VEHICLE_ARRIVED",
  "vehicle_id": "VH-501",
  "vehicle_type": "TRUCK",
  "sequence_no": 1501,
  "timestamp": "2026-10-08T10:15:20Z"
}

### 7. Vehicle cleared
POST {{host}}/api/sensor-events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "event_id": "evt-10002",
  "junction_id": "A",
  "direction": "NORTH",
  "event_type": "VEHICLE_CLEARED",
  "vehicle_id": "VH-501",
  "sequence_no": 1502,
  "timestamp": "2026-10-08T10:16:10Z"
}

### 8. Emergency vehicle from EAST (forces safe preemption)
POST {{host}}/api/sensor-events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "event_id": "evt-20001",
  "junction_id": "A",
  "direction": "EAST",
  "event_type": "VEHICLE_ARRIVED",
  "vehicle_id": "AMB-1",
  "vehicle_type": "EMERGENCY",
  "sequence_no": 2001,
  "timestamp": "2026-10-08T10:20:00Z"
}

### 9. Manual green request (an INTENT; the engine decides the safe transition)
POST {{host}}/api/junctions/{{junction}}/commands
Content-Type: application/json

{ "command": "MANUAL_GREEN_REQUEST", "direction": "WEST" }

### 10. Return to automatic
POST {{host}}/api/junctions/{{junction}}/commands
Content-Type: application/json

{ "command": "RETURN_TO_AUTOMATIC" }

### 11. Controller acknowledgement (take command_id from status.pending_command)
POST {{host}}/api/controller-events
Content-Type: application/json

{ "command_id": "cmd-REPLACE-ME", "junction_id": "A", "status": "ACK" }

### 12. Controller reports a DIFFERENT state than requested (mismatch -> retry -> degraded)
POST {{host}}/api/controller-events
Content-Type: application/json

{ "command_id": "cmd-REPLACE-ME", "junction_id": "A", "status": "ACK", "actual_state": "RED" }

### 13. Controller goes offline
POST {{host}}/api/device-status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "event_id": "status-301", "junction_id": "A", "device_type": "SIGNAL_CONTROLLER", "status": "OFFLINE", "timestamp": "2026-10-08T10:30:00Z" }

### 14. Controller back online (engine asks for a confirmed ALL_RED before resuming)
POST {{host}}/api/device-status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "event_id": "status-302", "junction_id": "A", "device_type": "SIGNAL_CONTROLLER", "status": "ONLINE", "timestamp": "2026-10-08T10:31:00Z" }

### 15. Sensor offline (engine assumes demand for that direction)
POST {{host}}/api/device-status
Content-Type: application/json

{ "event_id": "status-303", "junction_id": "A", "device_type": "SENSOR", "direction": "SOUTH", "status": "OFFLINE", "timestamp": "2026-10-08T10:32:00Z" }

### 16. History (newest first)
GET {{host}}/api/junctions/{{junction}}/history?limit=50

### 17. Demo helper: stop the simulated controller from answering (ACK never received)
POST {{host}}/api/simulator/auto-ack
Content-Type: application/json

{ "auto_ack": false }

### 18. Invalid examples (expect 400 / 404 / 422)
POST {{host}}/api/sensor-events
Content-Type: application/json

{ "event_id": "bad-1", "junction_id": "A", "direction": "UP", "event_type": "VEHICLE_ARRIVED", "vehicle_id": "X", "vehicle_type": "BICYCLE", "sequence_no": 1, "timestamp": "2026-10-08T10:00:00Z" }

###
GET {{host}}/api/junctions/NOPE/status
